  "hints": [
    "<p>For a fixed <code>k</code>, transform each <code>nums[i]</code> into <code>nums[i]</code> if it is divisible by <code>k</code>, and into <code>-nums[i]</code> otherwise.</p>",
    "<p>After this transformation, the best range <code>[l, r]</code> is the maximum subarray sum of the transformed array.</p>",
    "<p>It is enough to check values of <code>k</code> that divide at least one element of <code>nums</code>. Also handle <code>k = 2</code> for cases where no element is divisible by any chosen <code>k</code>.</p>",
    "<p>Enumerate all divisors greater than one from the elements of <code>nums</code>, and run Kadane's algorithm for each candidate <code>k</code>.</p>",
    "<p>When comparing candidates, maximize the score difference first, then choose the smaller <code>k</code> in case of a tie.</p>"
